Do US sanctions still work?






                In late August, US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent announced an 'Economic D-Day' against Iran that would place sanctions on all entities trading with the Islamic Republic.&nbsp;

In the latest episode of The Big Picture, Economics Editor at The Times Mehreen Khan explained why the new measures are unlikely to prove effective...

Hormuz ship crossings drop to four 






                Vessel transits through the Strait of Hormuz have dropped to four on&nbsp;Tuesday, down from seven a day earlier and the 10-day average of 18, according to&nbsp;preliminary shipping data from Kpler.&nbsp;

Two ships reportedly exiting the waterway and two other were entering.

US warns citizens to reconsider travel to Saudi Arabia






                The US has changed its travel advisory for Saudi Arabia to Level 3 amid the kingdom's escalating conflict with Yemen.&nbsp;

The US State Department’s international travel website warned of several risks under the "reconsider travel" advisory, including armed conflict,&nbsp;missile and drone attacks...

At least 11 killed from building collapse in Gaza City, dozens remain missing






                The bodies of at least 11 Palestinians have been recovered after a building sheltering displaced families&nbsp;collapsed west of Gaza City, with dozens remain missing.&nbsp;

